---
// The one call to action on every Journey B page, and it is a quote and not a
// booking. Rule 3 of plan section 1.1a: a stranger comparing IT providers
// will not give up half an hour before they know roughly what it costs.
//
// It is a component, not a block on each page, because there are three
// Journey B pages and one quote ask (XFO-68). Copied three times, the three
// would drift -- and XFO-78 would have three places to swap instead of one.
//
// XFO-46 builds the form itself. Its managed IT journey asks for four facts
// beyond name, company and email -- users, devices, current provider and cover
// needed. This block asks for a fifth: the number of offices. That is not
// padding. The price has a per-site fee in it, so a quote cannot be worked out
// from a headcount alone, and XFO-78 -- the issue that swaps this block for
// the real form -- has to add that field or the form collects a number we
// cannot quote from. When it lands, the <div class="quote-ask"> below is
// replaced by its <form data-enquiry-form> with journey "managed-it", and
// nothing else on any of the three pages changes.
---

<section class="clean-block clean-form" id="quote" aria-labelledby="quote-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="block-heading">
			<h2 id="quote-heading" class="text-info">Get a price for your business</h2>
			<p>You get a figure, not a sales process. If we are not the right fit we will say so.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="quote-ask">
			<p>Send us these five things and we will come back with a monthly price:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>How many people need support</li>
				<li>How many offices they sit in</li>
				<li>How many computers, laptops and servers you have</li>
				<li>Who looks after your IT today, if anyone</li>
				<li>The hours you need covered</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="mb-0">
				Email <a href="mailto:support@xfour.co.uk">support@xfour.co.uk</a> or call
				<a href="tel:+441183702920">0118 370 2920</a> and ask for a managed IT quote.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	/* The theme caps .block-heading p at 420px, which is too narrow here. */
	.block-heading p {
		max-width: 680px;
	}

	.quote-ask {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.quote-ask p,
	.quote-ask li {
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.quote-ask ol {
		padding-left: 1.3rem;
	}

	.quote-ask li {
		margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
	}
</style>
